Purpose: Convert the existing ScanSafe.AI prototype into a secure, reliable, scalable Android product and backend.
Capacity objective: Verify support for 10,000+ concurrent users under defined workloads.
Status: Engineering requirements to implement and test—not a claim that these requirements are already met.
1. Mission and non-negotiable rules
Inspect the actual repository before rewriting anything. Preserve working features and the approved visual design. Replace demo-only behavior with real implementations, close security gaps, add automated tests, and demonstrate capacity using repeatable load tests.
- Do not claim zero downtime, perfect security, or 10,000-user capacity without evidence.
- Do not leave mock data, hard-coded reports, fake authentication, or dummy billing in production paths.
- Never embed backend/database/AI secrets in the Android APK or commit secrets to source control.
- Treat OCR, model output, external APIs, and user-provided label text as untrusted input.
- Do not turn a timeout, missing match, or unavailable evidence source into a “safe” or “unsafe” conclusion.
- Implement incrementally with tests, reviewable changes, monitoring, and rollback plans.
- If credentials, provider access, source data, or decisions are missing, document the blocker instead of pretending it is resolved.
